'''VERTEX Esports Club''' is an [[:category:Australia|Australian]] esports organization that is a subsidiary of [[:category:Australia|Australian]] tournament organizer Australian Esports Network. They entered the ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' scene on March 12th, 2020 with the signing of [[4 and a half men]].

==Timeline==
{{tabs dynamic
|name1=2020
|name2=2021
|name3=2022
|name4=2023
|name5=2024
|This=5
|content1=
*March 12th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' enter ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' with the signing of [[4 and a half men]], a roster consisting of: [[willyKS]], [[Vexite]], [[toM]], [[soju_j]], and [[tensai]]. <ref name="first lineup">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1238001628101218306|date=2020-03-12|title=We are extremely proud to announce the newest addition to the #wolfpack!|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*May 22nd - [[Vexite]] and [[soju_j]] are acquired by [[Chiefs Esports Club]]. <ref name="may 2020">{{cite web|url=http://chiefsesc.com/welcome-zeph-soju-vexite/|date=2020-05-22|title=Zeph, Soju, & Vexite join Chiefs CSGO|publisher=[[Chiefs Esports Club]]}}</ref>
*July 7th - '''VERTEX Esports Club'''<nowiki>'s</nowiki> lineup disbands. <ref name="first disband">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/tensai_cs/status/1280426566544093185|date=2020-07-07|title=Vertex has parted ways and I am currently looking for a team to grind the next season|author=[[tensai]]}}</ref>
*August 25th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' sign a new lineup consisting of [[willyKS]], [[pz]], [[tensai]], [[Roflko]], and [[BRACE]]. <ref name="2nd lineup">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1298175783978950657|date=2020-08-25|title=A secret no more!|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*September 4th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' part ways with [[willyKS]]. <ref name="-willyks">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/willyKS11/status/1301852516951314433|date=2020-09-04|title=Left Vertex unfortunately things did not work out, best of luck to the boys|author=[[willyKS]]}}</ref>
*September 23rd - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' sign [[ADDICT]]. <ref name="+ADDICT">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1308676478897287168|date=2020-09-23|title=We are proud to OFFICIALLY announce @addicts_csgo will be joining our CS:GO roster!|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*December 19th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' sign [[soju_j]] as coach. <ref name="soju coach">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/vertexesc/status/1340230810700410880?s=21|title=Our final piece of the puzzle is finally OFFICIAL!|date=2020-12-19|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>

|content2=
*January 24th - [[Roflko]] retires from ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' and leaves '''VERTEX Esports Club''' in part because of his [[Banned_Players/ESIC|ESIC ban]]. <ref name="roflko retires">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Roflko/status/1353263707267227648|title=The end of my Journey in CS GO <3 Love you all|date=2021-01-24|author=[[Roflko]]}}</ref>
*March 3rd - [[tensai]] steps down from '''VERTEX Esports Club'''. <ref name="-tensai">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/tensai_cs/status/1367075078257655815|title=Parted ways with @VertexESC|date=2021-03-03|author=[[tensai]]}}</ref>
*March 8th - [[soju_j]] is acquired by [[Dire Wolves]]. <ref name="soju dire wolves">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/DireWolves/status/1368758375043854336|title=It might just be the name talking, but we think this guy can hit shots!|date=2021-03-08|author=[[Dire Wolves]]}}</ref>
*April 21st - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' sign [[Roflko]] and [[apocdud]]. <ref name="vertex +roflko/apocdud">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1384791498034614274|title=The worst kept secret in AU/NZ CS:GO is FINALLY official!|date=2021-04-21|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>

|content3=
*February 22nd - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' release [[ADDICT]]. <ref name="-addict">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1496030921987923970|title=It is with great displeasure that today we officially announce the release of @addicts_csgo from our CS:GO roster|date=2022-02-22|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*February 27th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' sign [[malta]]. <ref name="+malta">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1497807053750153218|title=But we felt we needed a bit more, so please welcome @malta_CS as our newest addition to the CSGO roster!|date=2022-02-27|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*June 26th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' part ways with [[Roflko]] and [[apocdud]]. <ref name="-Roflko">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Roflko/status/1540949188653248514|title=I have been removed from @VertexESC|date=2022-06-26|author=[[Roflko]]}}</ref><ref name="-apocdud">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/apocdud/status/1540950521845932032|title=Unfortunately I've been removed from @VertexESC|date=2022-06-26|author=[[apocdud]]}}</ref>
*July 4th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' sign [[Vexite]] and [[Valiance (Australian player)|Valiance]]. <ref name="+Vexite +Valiance">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1543848331532800002|title=The new and improved VERTEX CS:GO roster|date=2022-07-04|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*August 6th - [[Valiance (Australian player)|Valiance]] steps down from '''VERTEX Esports Club''' and takes an indefinite break from competitive ''[[CS:GO]]''. <ref name="-Valiance">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1555837866538057728|title=Although his stay was only short, Matt has shown us why he belongs at the top|date=2022-08-06|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*August 14th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' part ways with [[Vexite]]. <ref name="-Vexite">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1558755315167813633|title=Thank you @vexite_|date=2022-08-14|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*September 1st - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' re-sign [[ADDICT]]. <ref name="+ADDICT 2">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1565242069391908864|title=@addicts_csgo rejoins the #wolfpack |date=2022-09-01|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*November 11th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' acquire [[SaVage]] from [[Encore Esports Club]]. <ref name="+SaVage">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1590958005675524096|title="We've had our eye on you for some time"|date=2022-11-11|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>

|content4=
*February 7th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' part ways with [[SaVage]]. <ref name="-SaVage">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1622836509736050689|title=We regret to inform that VERTEX CS has parted ways with @SaVagecs_|date=2023-02-07|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*February 13th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' sign [[HaZR]] from [[Encore Esports Club]]. <ref name="+HaZR">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1625058875211939841|title=The boys decided to try a different approach to find their new 5th|date=2023-02-13|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*August 19th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' add [[Kingfisher]] as coach. <ref name="kingfisher coach">{{inside source|source=Kingfisher}}</ref>
*October 26th - [[malta]] retires from competitive ''Counter-Strike'' and leaves the team. <ref name="malta retire">{{cite_web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1717420801853403561|title=It is with a heavy heart that today, we announce that @malta_CS will be stepping away from VERTEX and competitive Counter-Strike|date=2023-10-26|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
*November 5th - [[Kingfisher]] steps down from '''VERTEX Esports Club'''. <ref name="-kingfisher">{{cite_web|url=https://twitter.com/Kingfisheroce/status/1721014713067479185|title=I'm taking an extended break from coaching/analysis to focus on life outside of team CS|date=2023-11-05|author=[[Kingfisher]]}}</ref>
*November 19th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' sign [[Valiance (Australian player)|Valiance]]. <ref name="valiance returns">{{cite_web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1726076293253628052|title=HES BACK|date=2023-11-19|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>

|content5=
*January 10th - '''VERTEX Esports Club''' close its ''Counter-Strike 2'' division. <ref name="-CS2">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VertexESC/status/1744953563732984200|title=The end of an era|date=2024-01-10|author='''VERTEX Esports Club'''}}</ref>
}}

